From: =?utf-8?b?Ik1hcmNvIFRyZXZpc2FuIChUcmV2acOxbyki?= <mail@3v1n0.net>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:00:45 +0200
Subject: tests: Make mock logind report the session as active

Since GNOME/gnome-session@dc497507e, gsm-systemd no longer queries
libsystemd directly for the session's active state.
Instead it finds the graphical session id via libsystemd on the host,
looks it up on the login1 service with GetSession(), and reads the
"Active" property from the returned object to decide whether the session
is active.

Our mock logind implements GetSession() by simply returning the object
path "/org/freedesktop/login1/session/<id>" without creating the object
behind it. As a result gnome-session's proxy fails to fetch the "Active"
property, the session is treated as inactive, and SessionIsActive on
org.gnome.SessionManager stays false.

The power plugin honors this and refuses idle mode transitions
("ignoring state transition to blank as inactive"), so the screensaver
blank tests time out waiting for the screen to blank.

We cannot predict which host session id gnome-session will discover, so
override GetSession() to lazily create an active session object for
whatever id is requested and return its path. This makes gnome-session
consider the session active again, as the tests expect.

Origin: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-settings-daemon/-/merge_requests/489
---
 tests/gsdtestcase.py | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/gsdtestcase.py b/tests/gsdtestcase.py
index ce75778..10b4629 100644
--- a/tests/gsdtestcase.py
+++ b/tests/gsdtestcase.py
@@ -287,6 +287,24 @@ class GSDTestCase(DBusTestCase):
             'self.props["org.freedesktop.login1.Manager"]["OnExternalPower"] = args[0]'
         )
 
+        # gnome-session (gsm-systemd) finds the graphical session id via
+        # libsystemd on the *host*, then looks it up on this (mocked) login1
+        # service via GetSession() and reads the returned object's "Active"
+        # property to decide whether the session is active (SessionIsActive).
+        #
+        # Since we can't predict which host session id gnome-session will find,
+        # override GetSession() so that it lazily creates an active session
+        # object for whatever id is requested, and returns its path. This makes
+        # gnome-session consider the session active, which several tests rely on.
+        self.logind_obj.AddMethod(
+            'org.freedesktop.login1.Manager', 'GetSession', 's', 'o',
+            'session_path = "/org/freedesktop/login1/session/" + args[0]\n'
+            'if session_path not in objects:\n'
+            '    self.AddSession(args[0], "seat0", %d, "%s", True)\n'
+            'ret = session_path'
+            % (os.getuid(), os.environ.get('USER', 'user'))
+        )
+
     def stop_logind(self):
         '''stop mock logind'''
 
